WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.687
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.987 --> 00:00:09.605
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.905 --> 00:00:15.425
Unit thirty-two: Whatever, However, No Matter. Today you will say that something does not matter.

4
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:18.262
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.584
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.381
Whatever.

7
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:27.336
Whatever means any thing at all.

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.915
Whatever you decide, I agree.

9
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:32.739
Your turn. Say: Whatever.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.543
Whatever.

11
00:00:37.283 --> 00:00:38.180
Whenever.

12
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:40.777
Whenever means at any time.

13
00:00:41.383 --> 00:00:42.570
Come whenever you like.

14
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:45.545
Your turn. Say: Whenever.

15
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.355
Whenever.

16
00:00:50.117 --> 00:00:51.083
Wherever.

17
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:54.071
Wherever means in any place.

18
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:56.718
Wherever he goes, he smiles.

19
00:00:57.317 --> 00:00:59.505
Your turn. Say: Wherever.

20
00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.368
Wherever.

21
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:05.048
However.

22
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.632
However means in any way.

23
00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:09.775
However hard I try...

24
00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:12.780
Your turn. Say: However.

25
00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:16.460
However.

26
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:18.009
Whoever.

27
00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:20.819
Whoever means any person.

28
00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:23.463
Whoever called, didn't leave a message.

29
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.609
Your turn. Say: Whoever.

30
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.375
Whoever.

31
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:32.048
No matter.

32
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.212
No matter means it is not important.

33
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:37.468
No matter what happens.

34
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.852
Your turn. Say: No matter.

35
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.724
No matter.

36
00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:46.415
Anything.

37
00:01:47.417 --> 00:01:48.871
Anything means any thing.

38
00:01:49.483 --> 00:01:50.914
Anything is possible.

39
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:53.879
Your turn. Say: Anything.

40
00:01:56.733 --> 00:01:57.653
Anything.

41
00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.511
Regardless.

42
00:02:00.517 --> 00:02:02.841
Regardless means without concern for.

43
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.032
Regardless of the cost.

44
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:08.687
Your turn. Say: Regardless.

45
00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:12.743
Regardless.

46
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.929
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.783 --> 00:02:22.314
Visal, complete the sentence: Whatever happens tomorrow, I…

48
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:34.036
Whatever happens tomorrow, I will stay calm. Whatever means it does not matter what. These words add -ever to question words, with the sense of any or no matter.

49
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.360
How are they used?

50
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:50.211
Whenever you call, I will answer. Wherever he goes, he makes friends. However hard I try, I can't win. Whoever called left no message. They begin a clause that shows no limit.

51
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:52.678
What about no matter?

52
00:02:53.783 --> 00:03:08.069
No matter what, no matter who, no matter how: No matter how tired I am, I exercise. It means the same as the -ever words, and regardless of is followed by a noun: regardless of the weather.

53
00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:11.140
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:16.514
Grammar focus: Whatever and whenever and however and no matter plus clause.

55
00:03:16.814 --> 00:03:18.152
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.558
Whatever happens tomorrow, I will stay calm.

57
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.542
However hard I try, I can't win.

58
00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.902
No matter how tired I am, I exercise.

59
00:03:28.867 --> 00:03:35.095
Whatever / whenever / wherever / however / whoever = any… No matter + question word has the same meaning. Regardless of + noun.

60
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.640
Be careful! Don't say: However you decide, I agree.

61
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.331
Say: Whatever you decide, I agree.

62
00:03:44.631 --> 00:03:45.980
Use whatever.

63
00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:49.210
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.257
It Doesn't Matter.

65
00:03:51.557 --> 00:03:54.102
Whatever happens tomorrow, I will stay calm.

66
00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.448
Wherever he goes, he makes new friends.

67
00:03:58.433 --> 00:04:01.129
However hard I try, I cannot win this game.

68
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:05.038
No matter how tired I am, I exercise every day.

69
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:08.370
Regardless of the weather, we will play.

70
00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:13.225
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.083 --> 00:04:16.408
blank you decide, I will support you.

72
00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:19.978
A, Whatever. B, Whenever. C, Wherever.

73
00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:25.486
The answer is A: Whatever.

74
00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.429
blank hard I try, I fail.

75
00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:32.498
A, Whatever. B, Whoever. C, However.

76
00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:38.161
The answer is C: However.

77
00:04:39.317 --> 00:04:41.293
blank of the cost, we will go.

78
00:04:41.593 --> 00:04:45.223
A, Regardless. B, No matter. C, However.

79
00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:51.509
The answer is A: Regardless.

80
00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.487
'No matter what' means blank.

81
00:04:54.787 --> 00:04:59.125
A, it matters what. B, what matters. C, it doesn't matter what.

82
00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:05.537
The answer is C: it doesn't matter what.

83
00:05:06.683 --> 00:05:10.424
According to the reading, what will they do regardless of the weather?

84
00:05:10.724 --> 00:05:14.262
A, play. B, stay home. C, cancel.

85
00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.358
The answer is A: play.

86
00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:23.614
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.413
Complete the sentence: 'Whatever happens tomorrow, I…'.

88
00:05:36.217 --> 00:05:38.239
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:51.492
Whatever happens tomorrow, I will keep trying. No matter how difficult the exam is, I will do my best. I use whatever and no matter to show that the result does not change my attitude.

90
00:05:51.792 --> 00:05:53.502
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.417 --> 00:06:00.378
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and whatever and whenever and however and no matter plus clause.

92
00:06:00.678 --> 00:06:04.793
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:06:05.093 --> 00:06:08.279
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.579 --> 00:06:11.243
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

